{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 2116, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an m x n grid. A robot starts at the top-left corner of the grid (0, 0) and wants to reach the bottom-right corner (m - 1, n - 1). The robot can move either right or down at any point in time.\nThe grid contains a value coins[i][j] in each cell:\n\nIf coins[i][j] >= 0, the robot gains that many coins.\nIf coins[i][j] < 0, the robot encounters a robber, and the robber steals the absolute value of coins[i][j] coins.\n\nThe robot has a special ability to neutralize robbers in at most 2 cells on its path, preventing them from stealing coins in those cells.\nNote: The robot's total coins can be negative.\nReturn the maximum profit the robot can gain on the route.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: coins = [[0,1,-1],[1,-2,3],[2,-3,4]]\nOutput: 8\nExplanation:\nAn optimal path for maximum coins is:\n\nStart at (0, 0) with 0 coins (total coins = 0).\nMove to (0, 1), gaining 1 coin (total coins = 0 + 1 = 1).\nMove to (1, 1), where there's a robber stealing 2 coins. The robot uses one neutralization here, avoiding the robbery (total coins = 1).\nMove to (1, 2), gaining 3 coins (total coins = 1 + 3 = 4).\nMove to (2, 2), gaining 4 coins (total coins = 4 + 4 = 8).\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: coins = [[10,10,10],[10,10,10]]\nOutput: 40\nExplanation:\nAn optimal path for maximum coins is:\n\nStart at (0, 0) with 10 coins (total coins = 10).\nMove to (0, 1), gaining 10 coins (total coins = 10 + 10 = 20).\nMove to (0, 2), gaining another 10 coins (total coins = 20 + 10 = 30).\nMove to (1, 2), gaining the final 10 coins (total coins = 30 + 10 = 40).\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\nm == coins.length\nn == coins[i].length\n1 <= m, n <= 500\n-1000 <= coins[i][j] <= 1000\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def maximumAmount(self, coins: List[List[int]]) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 2181, "char_start": 2128, "quote": "Input:\n[[0, 1, -1], [1, -2, 3], [2, -3, 4]]\nOutput:\n8", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 2239, "char_start": 2193, "quote": "Input:\n[[10, 10, 10], [10, 10, 10]]\nOutput:\n40", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "05b3864491f1015f25378e13c7032338a9a3983a1f2d7ca9418773a7f1a65cab", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "665559b1c3777575c83a7e3d23981ee3b8d101a3b4fe14f4131aa53c145a49ca", "seq": 2}
